00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.260
<i>Chiga Teruko</i>

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.260
<i>Youngest Triplet Maid</i>

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.890
...are triplets.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.640
Exactly.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.810
And, well...just a feeling, I suppose.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.400
I never almost never saw Rei doing any work.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.150
I wondered why...and, well...

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.570
I served you tea!

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.740
It was excellent.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.580
Also...yeah.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:14.000
The first time I visited your room, you were
on the sofa, and 'Ilia' was standing up.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:18.010
That seemed like it should be the other way around.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:23.760
Go on.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.850
Er...well...

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.270
Right.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:34.110
The deciding factor was that fake Ilia defended you.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:39.820
Oh...I suppose I should speak for myself here.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:45.370
I was talking to Rei in my room all night.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.370
Isn't that right, Rei?

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:54.080
Anyway, she didn't defend Hikari at all.
In fact, she accused her being the killer.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.000
But where Rei had no alibi, she lied, and made one for her.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.340
Why?

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.390
Because Rei was closer to her than Hikari?

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:05.890
Maybe.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.020
But I wasn't satisfied with that answer.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:15.230
People living together on an island that isolated...
seems like you'd pretty much have to get close.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.110
I just don't think humans are that cold.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.530
Very true.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:25.700
They are all like my family.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:31.450
The precious family that stayed with me
even when I was exiled here.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:37.290
But 'Ilia' did defend Rei, and did not defend Hikari.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:38.790
Why?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:44.010
What if Rei was more important that Ilia herself?

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.390
Someone she had sworn loyalty to?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.220
Seemed like a decent possibility, anyway.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.480
Very well done. I could almost hug you.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:55.770
I don't mind.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:56.900
I can resist.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.280
May I ask...

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.360
Why did you switch places with Rei and pretend to be a maid?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.820
I wanted to know who would be the first to notice.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.950
Almost a prank, really. No other reason for it.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.500
A prank?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:19.670
That was a bit disappointing, somehow, but it was also probably true.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:27.640
It just happened that none of these
so-called geniuses had ever picked up on it.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.430
Hey...are you sure you won't come back to the mansion?

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:39.440
Kunagisa, Maki, Yayoi, and you.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.360
All four of you could become part of my little family.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.860
I can't stand murderers.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.910
No matter what the reason?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.410
No matter what the reason.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:54.790
Right.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:59.380
I don't know what Hikari or Teruko told you, but...

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:05.550
I'm sure you don't think that everything they said was true.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.260
Maybe.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:11.470
The reason I didn't call the police was quite simple.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.100
Doing so would be no fun at all!

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:19.020
Authority is soooo tiresome.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.020
Goodbye, then.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.200
Hoo boy.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.580
Jesus...I'm a fool.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.460
Almost there.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:54.970
Family?

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:59.600
Should I really have turned that down?

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.520
Nonsense.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:16.580
<i>Days Later вЂ“ The Red Red Fantasia</i>

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.250
I had finally started college...

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.540
But since I'd completely missed the start of term it didn't really take.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.840
I'd left school after morning classes, and was walking down Nishi-oji.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:34.470
Kyoto

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.300
Cutting class. Ditching school.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:39.890
Came all the way back to Japan for what, exactly?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.560
Or is that more nonsense?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:52.070
Oh, right, that magazine Kunagisa likes comes out today.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.580
Kunagisa had not left her apartment since.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:09.590
She was busy rebuilding the computers
and workstations Akane smashed.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:16.140
She'd also checked up on Sonoyama Akane and Sakaki Shinya.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:29.570
Akane had quit the Seven Fools, and was leading a more
secluded life...while retaining her reputation as an academic.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.990
Shinya had stayed with her.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:38.700
Since we never called the police, that was all there was to it.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.030
You really don't close your eyes.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:17.490
Pretty damn cool. Bad ass, even.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.440
Well. Okay.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:21.330
Hello.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:22.750
Hello?

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.580
Did I tell you to say hello?

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.260
Who...<i>are</i> you?

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.060
My name's Aikawa Jun.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.020
Aikawa?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.020
Call me Jun.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:54.490
Um, Jun. Have we ever met before?

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.740
First time.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.660
...thought so.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.910
What, didn't Ilia tell you anything?

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:02.910
Ilia?

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:10.500
So you're Aikawa вЂ“ the detective?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.840
More accurately, I'm a consultant.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.050
Looks like you remember me now.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.760
I was on my way to your college!

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:23.180
Then I spotted you browsing in the bookstore.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.020
Stroke of luck, I thought. Stopped to chat.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.310
So...you were looking for me?

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:36.780
Yeah. Wanted to see the face of the man
who had the nerve to steal a job from me.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:43.240
I blew my entrance because of you! I never even
<i>had</i> an entrance! You'd better make it up to me.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:53.210
I lost a job because of you! Sure, it was a pissant little job.
Just using my brain a minute, no risk to life or limb.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:55.340
Um...

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.090
I'm sorry, I guess. My bad.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:06.390
Don't apologize! Gave me a vacation. I oughta be thanking you.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:15.860
So I've had a look at you. One order of business taken care of! One to go.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.480
Um...

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.360
What's the other one? Exactly?

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:21.490
Well...

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.040
I thought I'd clear up what's troubling you.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.830
Um...what is it that troubles me?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.460
Take a guess!

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.670
<i>I</i> came to see you.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.380
<i>Me.</i>

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:40.800
Gotta be that mess on Wet Wing Raven Island, right?

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.640
The murder?

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.430
Yup.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.350
Were you not satisfied, Aikawa?

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:50.600
Jun.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.610
Never use my last name.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.980
Only people that do...

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.150
...are my enemies.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.150
Consultant really is
the best possible word
for this, can't fathom
why anyone would use
anything else at all

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.150
<i>Aikawa Jun</i>

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.150
<i>Humanity's Strongest
Consultant</i>

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.700
I stopped by the island.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:10.580
I heard how things went down. Ilia, Hikari, Akari, and Rei all filled me in.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.080
You solved the case.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.840
You solved it beyond argument.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.670
But it bugs you, doesn't it?

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.800
Your solution doesn't feel quite right?

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.140
She was right.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:36.650
Kunagisa and I had ignored any number of details that didn't fit in order to solve the case as fast as possible.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:42.440
And offered up deductions that, deep down, bothered me.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:51.410
You know what it is? You know what bugs you,
what bothers you, what makes you so damn unsatisfied?

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.000
Well...um...

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.960
Why would Shinya kill Ibuki?

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:05.340
Why would Shinya and Sonoyama work together?

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.550
Am I right?

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.270
You are.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:17.810
But that's their problem, and nothing more than their problem.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.820
Anything related to their motive...

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:24.950
Anything around that...that's out of my hands.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.240
He's like you.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.320
You thought so yourself.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:31.080
Shinya himself said as much.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.410
You and Sakaki Shinya are a lot alike.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:41.590
To him, Ibuki Kanami was irreplaceable.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:46.050
Same as the blue-haired kid is to you.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:48.180
How could he kill her?

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.180
I guess I was just wrong.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.060
If not...then, well.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:59.020
Then it was actually Akane that mattered to him.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.320
You happy with that answer?

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:06.650
Course you aren't! You're miserable with that answer!

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.830
I can feel it oozing off of you! I know everything you feel.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.910
But what other explanation is there?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:24.050
When you eliminate the impossible, whatever
remains, however improbable, must be the truth.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.800
That's just superstition.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:33.890
So, what, did you believe that bullshit
about her wanting to eat people's brains?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:39.980
So what do you make of it, Jun?

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.940
You've figured it all out?

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:46.110
Then please, tell me.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:51.950
If you'd asked me right off the bat, you'd have saved us all some time.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:58.410
Hikari told me. You noticed, didn't you?

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:04.460
The painting you modeled for. Why was there a watch?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.720
This painting seem odd to you?

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:11.800
You meet the painting of you?

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.100
What? Looks normal to me.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.980
Grab a shot of it, please. Something's bugging me.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:23.980
The watch? That...I'd completely...

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:25.400
...forgotten.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:29.030
You didn't forget, did you?

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:31.030
Absolutely not.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:32.700
How could I?

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:38.120
But...I assumed she made a mistake.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:43.000
Kanami relied on her memory to draw.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:46.380
She just...remembered wrong. And...

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:47.880
Poppycock.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:52.720
This lady said crazy shit like, "Memory and perception are the same."

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:55.510
She's functionally incapable of a mistake like that.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:58.810
Maybe it is technically possible. But bro...

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:03.270
There's another reason here. Don't you agree?

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:04.900
Then, Ai--

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.270
Jun. What is that reason?

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.900
I can't speak for anyone else...

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:16.160
But as Humanity's Strongest Consultant,
I, Aikawa Jun, solemnly declare...

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:20.000
...that Ibuki Kanami did not paint that painting.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:22.960
Right?

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.880
Only explanation.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.090
Reductio ad absurdum.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:32.380
Say Ibuki drew the picture. Then it makes
no sense for the watch to be in the picture.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.090
Right?

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:37.430
You weren't wearing the watch when you posed for her.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.430
Therefore, she wasn't the one who painted the watch.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:42.230
But...how?

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:47.310
"How?" Dude, you didn't see her paint the thing.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.030
I drew one conclusion.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.780
Ibuki couldn't paint.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.820
"Couldn't"?

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.450
Kanami was an artist!

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.080
A famous one.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.200
Of course she could paint!

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.040
How so?

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:07.380
Plenty of fake artists using ghost painters to do their work.

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.500
Then Kanami was one of those fakes?

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.510
Can you draw?

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:17.510
I'm not...very artistic.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:28.730
Knowing you, I bet you just thought, "Wow, Ibuki
Kanami's a real artist's artist," or something equally dumb.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:35.400
Exactly why did you think Ibuki was an artist?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:38.740
Why? Well...I guess...

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:42.620
You never actually saw her draw, right?

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.160
You just heard her talk about it.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:50.790
And you decided she was an artist based purely on what she said.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:54.590
I saw the sketch! Of the cherry blossoms.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:56.880
But not her drawing it.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:02.430
Bro. For someone who doesn't trust anyone you sure are gullible.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:08.440
You may not trust them but you don't bother doubting
anything, or just don't bother making up your mind.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:12.020
You just swallowed Ibuki's bluff whole.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.860
Bluff? That was a bluff?

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:20.530
Everything she said to me was a bluff? Really?

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.420
Ibuki Kanami, the genius artist who couldn't paint.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:32.840
How would you resolve this contradiction?

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:40.300
Okay, um...so like you said, Kanami wasn't a real painter?

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:44.600
No. Think! And figure it out, kid.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:51.810
That painting wasn't drawn by Ibuki. But Ibuki
<i>was</i> an artist. So simple logic tells us one thing!

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:53.520
<i>That</i> Ibuki was a fake.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.820
Therefore...<i>of course</i> she couldn't draw!

00:18:58.490 --> 00:18:59.200
A fake?

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.160
But is she was fake...

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.490
Why...?

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:07.370
Um. Sorry, I'm confused.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.250
So...you mean...

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:17.840
The fake Kanami was murdered, and the real Kanami wasn't?

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:22.640
Yep. And the real Sonoyama Akane <i>was</i> murdered.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:24.470
WHAT!?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:25.970
Akane was...!?

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.980
Yes. Sonoyama Akane.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.600
Explains the first question, doesn't it?

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:35.770
Why would Shinya kill Ibuki?

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:37.030
Simple.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.820
<i>He didn't.</i>

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:42.660
Why would Shinya and Sonoyama work together?

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:43.740
Simple.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:45.620
<i>They didn't.</i>

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:49.500
He worked with Ibuki Kanami. His one and only.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:54.710
Kanami and Akane switched places? When!?

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.340
Hold on...

00:19:56.750 --> 00:20:00.380
I was on the same island as them for three days!

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:04.220
Even with my memory, I'd notice if they switched places!

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:08.180
So they must have switched before that.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.180
Before the island.

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.810
Ibuki Kanami. Sonoyama Akane.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:17.860
I don't know how long they were on the island, but...before that.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.070
Blonde, blue-eyed. The other a brainy brunette.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.650
Explain that!

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:26.660
You can dye hair. You can wear color contacts.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:30.160
If you want to look like someone else, it ain't that hard.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:34.330
Particularly if they've got a shtick that's easy to identify.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.790
But...the painting?

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:39.710
Sonoyama painted it.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:44.970
When you talked to her, you were wearing the watch, right?

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.800
So Sonoyama must have painted you.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.560
And by Sonoyama I mean the real Ibuki.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:54.230
Sonoyama Akane...was Ibuki Kanami...

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:58.940
Come to think of it, where <i>was</i> Akane been all morning?

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:02.820
Why...do that?

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:08.330
To convince you that Sonoyama as Ibuki was Ibuki.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:13.540
Who would ever suspect that it wasn't
actually Ibuki Kanami who painted the thing?

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:20.300
Though I gotta say, the watch was
an uncharacteristically careless mistake.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.970
But...but Ilia!

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:28.640
Ilia invited them. Didn't she notice?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.220
Why would she?

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:33.770
But...she must have seen a photo or something.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:35.190
A photo?

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.190
Don't make me laugh.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:42.440
Do you actually think people look like their photographs?

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:46.740
No, you meet them in the flesh and they seem totally different.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.820
Photos don't move. Reality does.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:54.330
And human eyes are not exactly objective. All there is to it.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:59.290
You compare a photo to the real person, and you believe the person.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:02.170
But why? Why would they...?

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:05.380
A prank. For the fun of it.

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:10.180
Just to see if anyone would notice.
Would any of these geniuses work it out?

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:16.850
Would the rich girl who invites so many geniuses
to her salon be able to tell them apart?

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:22.190
At least, that's what Sonoyama believed.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:24.610
Oh...the real one.

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:30.820
Shinya and Ibuki contacted her, and
proposed the plan. Sonoyama agreed.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:33.740
Bet she thought it sounded fun.

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:37.370
Academics are more up for that sort of thing than you'd expect.

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:42.840
Particularly the ER3 System type. As you know only too well.

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:44.670
They took advantage of that.

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:46.920
Chee-kun's intel.

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:50.720
They met in Chicago. Ibuki Kanami and Sonoyama Akane.

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:52.720
They knew each other.

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:56.060
Well enough to have planned something like this.

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:59.190
All those fights the two of them had...

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:04.690
Those were all staged to make sure we
never noticed they'd switched places?

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:09.200
Okay, so...then what?

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:10.570
Easy.

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:16.160
Ibuki and Sonoyama switched places. Ibuki
became Sonoyama. Sonoyama became Ibuki.

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:21.710
And one of the two was murdered. Sonoyama
remained. The one who had become Sonoyama.

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:27.800
If you thought she was dead once, then found out she was actually the killer...

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:32.800
who's gonna wonder if she was actually someone else entirely?

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:36.850
So Kanami...<i>became</i> Akane?

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:41.560
Since you didn't turn her over to the police...

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:44.940
So <i>that</i> was her motive?

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:48.570
By why would she do that?

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:56.700
Never though I'd hear a question that staggeringly dull from you!

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:58.330
Hey, bro.

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:02.830
If I asked you what you live for, how would you answer?

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:11.590
Yeah, your type never even thinks to wonder.

00:24:12.090 --> 00:24:17.810
You've never thought about what you want to be.
You've never thought about <i>who</i> you want to be.

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:23.350
No matter how much I explain, you'll never
understand Ibuki Kanami's feelings.

00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:30.780
You're complete the way you are. You could travel
the whole damn world and never understand her.

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:34.070
You sound like <i>you</i> understand.

00:24:34.280 --> 00:24:37.870
No way. How could I understand how someone else thinks?

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:42.370
But I got a brain. I can<i> imagine</i>.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:49.750
She shed her old skin, 'Ibuki', and was reborn as 'Sonoyama.'

00:24:50.580 --> 00:24:53.940
With all the advantages being Sonoyama Akane came with.

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:56.760
But...won't anyone notice?

00:24:56.760 --> 00:24:58.080
Prolly not.

00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.800
She did her homework.

00:25:01.740 --> 00:25:08.360
They looked alike in the first place, or she'd never
have considered something as nuts as taking her place.

00:25:08.660 --> 00:25:10.080
Taking her place...

00:25:10.700 --> 00:25:12.820
She killed her to become her?

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:19.160
Certainly, you could never pull that off
with the original still running around...

00:25:19.160 --> 00:25:23.500
But she could have accomplished the same thing by just killing Ibuki.

00:25:24.080 --> 00:25:28.180
There was no reason to pretend she'd been murdered too.

00:25:28.180 --> 00:25:29.580
If she'd done that...

00:25:29.580 --> 00:25:35.080
People would have started looking for
a reason why <i>only</i> Ibuki was murdered.

00:25:35.080 --> 00:25:40.940
They needed to make it look serial.
To hide the real motive for the murder.

00:25:41.820 --> 00:25:45.440
They needed a deranged psycho hell bent on killing the lot of you.

00:25:45.620 --> 00:25:50.360
But it wasn't like she wanted to kill just anyone.

00:25:50.940 --> 00:25:53.860
That's why she pretended to be a victim.

00:25:53.860 --> 00:25:57.100
Clear as day. Right? Couldn't be clearer.

00:25:57.440 --> 00:26:01.440
Would a murderer really be reluctant to kill again?

00:26:01.680 --> 00:26:05.660
You know, not all murderers enjoy it.

00:26:06.060 --> 00:26:08.760
Just like not all wolves are lone wolves.

00:26:09.300 --> 00:26:13.560
They just minimized the risk required to achieve their goal.

00:26:13.560 --> 00:26:19.120
The more mysteries they create, the more
clues you have to work with, am I right?

00:26:19.740 --> 00:26:22.000
But they tried to kill Yayoi.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:23.100
But they <i>didn't</i>.

00:26:24.220 --> 00:26:25.980
You just <i>thought</i> they were.

00:26:26.340 --> 00:26:31.100
You just decided that Sonoyama Akane planned to kill more people!

00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:34.560
But you were wrong. That what we call biased thinking!

00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:39.980
Think. And figure it out, kid.

00:26:40.180 --> 00:26:44.200
You were dancing on the palms of their hands!

00:26:44.200 --> 00:26:46.860
Why did Shinya show you the sleeping bag?

00:26:46.860 --> 00:26:52.280
Why did Ibuki smash the computers when she
knew everyone was eating breakfast together?

00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:53.800
...it was all...?

00:26:59.200 --> 00:27:02.480
You fell for the picture they painted for you.

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:08.200
Just as they drew it, not even a wristwatch out of place.

00:27:08.180 --> 00:27:11.180
Maybe she was a bit of an artist after all!

00:27:12.820 --> 00:27:18.960
You know, they probably planned this all out for me, a week later.

00:27:19.320 --> 00:27:20.040
Wait...

00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:25.780
You can steal credentials, assume someone else's
identity...but there's still the problem of talent.

00:27:26.340 --> 00:27:33.740
Akane may have quit the Seven Fools, but she's still an
academic, still doing the same level of work as before.

00:27:34.220 --> 00:27:36.760
If the two of them had switched places...

00:27:36.760 --> 00:27:38.180
"If"?

00:27:40.040 --> 00:27:45.100
You still talking like that? You need to be more adaptable.

00:27:45.380 --> 00:27:49.960
Jun, if your theory is correct, 'Akane' is really Kanami in disguise.

00:27:50.380 --> 00:27:54.280
But Kunagisa checked up on her, and her output hasn't changed at all.

00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:55.540
Course not.

00:27:55.840 --> 00:28:02.880
She can paint, she can study, she can kill and
she can become someone else. You know why?

00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:05.200
She's a genius.

00:28:07.360 --> 00:28:08.220
A genius.

00:28:09.180 --> 00:28:12.100
Why had Ibuki been invited there?

00:28:12.660 --> 00:28:16.020
Because she had a unique ability.

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:21.820
She was unlike anyone else. She was better
than everyone else. She was the top of her field.

00:28:22.440 --> 00:28:26.220
That...that was <i>why</i>...

00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:31.080
How did you define genius?

00:28:31.380 --> 00:28:33.140
"Great people?"

00:28:33.140 --> 00:28:34.680
Ilia told me.

00:28:34.680 --> 00:28:36.600
But that's just wrong.

00:28:36.600 --> 00:28:38.780
You gotta think in terms of vectors.

00:28:39.540 --> 00:28:43.800
A genius is someone who pours themselves
into one thing, one direction in life.

00:28:44.420 --> 00:28:46.480
People can do all sorts of things.

00:28:46.480 --> 00:28:52.880
But if they don't do all sorts of things, if they concentrate on
one thing and one thing only, they can do all kinds of crazy shit.

00:28:52.880 --> 00:28:56.400
Shit that everyone else thinks is 'great'.

00:28:58.420 --> 00:28:59.840
Specialized functions.

00:29:00.120 --> 00:29:01.580
Focused vectors.

00:29:01.900 --> 00:29:03.100
Limited biases.

00:29:03.760 --> 00:29:09.800
Instead of splitting attention, they aimed it all in one direction.

00:29:10.540 --> 00:29:11.520
Concentrated.

00:29:12.020 --> 00:29:13.260
Savant syndrome.

00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:15.500
Insatiable appetite.

00:29:18.240 --> 00:29:20.000
You did well, kid!

00:29:20.440 --> 00:29:22.440
But you're still an amateur.

00:29:22.740 --> 00:29:31.420
You just weren't ready to end the story before
the detective showed up. You need a bit more training.

00:29:31.420 --> 00:29:33.620
But wait a second...

00:29:34.040 --> 00:29:36.420
Kanami was in a wheelchair!

00:29:36.420 --> 00:29:39.920
No reason you can't use a wheelchair with healthy legs!

00:29:40.200 --> 00:29:41.660
All there is to it.

00:29:41.660 --> 00:29:43.420
Legs are merely decorations.

00:29:43.420 --> 00:29:47.920
They come in handy for kicking your ass, but that's about all.

00:29:48.180 --> 00:29:52.080
That works for Akane. She just had to sit down.

00:29:52.700 --> 00:29:55.400
But Kanami was born with bad legs.

00:29:55.860 --> 00:29:58.000
She couldn't just stand up and--

00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:04.260
Ibuki Kanami? Who became Sonoyama Akane.
Who wanted to become someone else.

00:30:04.260 --> 00:30:10.780
If she was someone else <i>before</i> she became Ibuki,
I wouldn't be the least bit surprised.

00:30:12.960 --> 00:30:16.460
How long had Shinya been with Ibuki?

00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:18.920
A long time, he'd said.

00:30:19.220 --> 00:30:20.700
Just how long?

00:30:21.720 --> 00:30:24.660
He was with Akane now.

00:30:25.160 --> 00:30:26.920
For how long?

00:30:27.980 --> 00:30:29.080
A virtual machine.

00:30:29.420 --> 00:30:32.300
Machine after machine after machine.

00:30:32.580 --> 00:30:34.600
With no style to speak of.

00:30:34.880 --> 00:30:36.920
All styles rejected.

00:30:37.500 --> 00:30:39.320
That's...just...

00:30:40.280 --> 00:30:47.440
Had Maki... Had Himena Maki, the psychic, known?
Had she known this, too?

00:30:48.340 --> 00:30:54.240
And knowing it, watched things unfold, smiling, grinning?

00:30:54.900 --> 00:30:58.220
Just let it happen?

00:30:59.620 --> 00:31:00.720
What was real?

00:31:01.000 --> 00:31:02.080
What was a lie?

00:31:02.780 --> 00:31:04.200
Who was real?

00:31:04.200 --> 00:31:05.240
Who was a lie?

00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:08.600
Don't ask.

00:31:15.340 --> 00:31:16.760
Dust to dust.

00:31:17.600 --> 00:31:19.260
What's done is done.

00:31:20.080 --> 00:31:21.900
You did well, kid.

00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:24.960
Very well. Accept this praise.

00:31:25.860 --> 00:31:29.140
But you can do better.

00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:34.160
If something bothers you, figure out what.
If you're uncertain, make yourself certain.

00:31:34.460 --> 00:31:36.980
Push at shit till it makes sense.

00:31:37.640 --> 00:31:41.420
Do not dismiss what you feel as mere sentiment.

00:31:46.780 --> 00:31:47.780
Okay?

00:31:51.080 --> 00:31:51.760
Okay.

00:31:52.340 --> 00:31:53.660
Good!

00:31:57.180 --> 00:32:03.760
Then may you be well. The world's a worthwhile place
because people like you are in it. I think so, anyway.

00:32:04.260 --> 00:32:07.520
But dude, you've been slacking off a bit too much.

00:32:08.140 --> 00:32:12.660
Humans are meant for MUCH better things! Buckle down.

00:32:13.780 --> 00:32:16.520
That's all for today!

00:32:16.520 --> 00:32:18.620
Scram! Go on, get out!

00:32:20.940 --> 00:32:22.780
Kunagisa's apartment building...

00:32:26.180 --> 00:32:27.080
I see.

00:32:27.740 --> 00:32:30.300
Well, this certainly is heaven.

00:32:30.300 --> 00:32:32.080
Or maybe hell.

00:32:33.780 --> 00:32:36.380
You were on your way here anyway, right?

00:32:36.380 --> 00:32:37.620
How'd you know?

00:32:40.900 --> 00:32:42.900
Like a detective.

00:32:45.080 --> 00:32:47.300
See you again sometime.

00:32:47.300 --> 00:32:53.060
Weirdo like you's bound to run into me again.

00:32:53.360 --> 00:32:55.720
Say 'Hi' to Kunagisa for me.

00:32:55.900 --> 00:32:59.860
Come up and meet her. Since you're here already.

00:33:00.440 --> 00:33:02.820
Nah, saw her yesterday.

00:33:06.020 --> 00:33:06.680
Jun.

00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:08.060
Then...

00:33:08.840 --> 00:33:09.620
Tell me...

00:33:10.140 --> 00:33:12.460
What do you live for?

00:33:12.460 --> 00:33:17.140
Do I need to say? Same as you, Ii-tan.

00:33:23.320 --> 00:33:26.380
Feels like I've been mugged.

00:33:28.240 --> 00:33:30.620
The metaphor was hardly inappropriate.

00:33:31.420 --> 00:33:37.160
She'd swiped all the baggage I'd been lugging
around, and left me feeling empty inside.

00:33:38.880 --> 00:33:40.940
Really. Honestly.

00:33:41.820 --> 00:33:44.440
Everything, and everyone.

00:33:47.340 --> 00:33:48.340
Really.

00:33:49.480 --> 00:33:50.860
Really.

00:33:51.820 --> 00:33:53.680
Unbelievable nonsense.

00:33:55.040 --> 00:33:56.640
Like Akagami Ilia.

00:33:57.420 --> 00:34:01.840
Gathering geniuses, mocking them, lying to them.

00:34:02.420 --> 00:34:06.420
All for her own pleasure, in her own little world.

00:34:07.040 --> 00:34:09.280
Now and forever.

00:34:10.620 --> 00:34:12.000
Like the Chiga triplets.

00:34:12.900 --> 00:34:17.640
All three identical and yet completely different.

00:34:18.280 --> 00:34:24.100
But like the Sierpinski triangle, they were fractal aspects of the whole...

00:34:24.620 --> 00:34:30.500
Their differences making them all the more alike,
the infinite depths of which no one would ever know.

00:34:32.040 --> 00:34:33.710
Text to cover
uuuuuup what lies
beneath thiiiis bit
we need one more

00:34:32.040 --> 00:34:33.710
<i>Himena Maki</i>

00:34:32.040 --> 00:34:33.710
<i>Genius - Fortune Teller</i>

00:34:32.340 --> 00:34:33.700
Like Himena Maki.

00:34:34.700 --> 00:34:43.580
She knew the truth, knew all truths, and
elected to yawn like a cat and go to sleep.

00:34:45.260 --> 00:34:46.680
Like Aikawa Jun.

00:34:47.480 --> 00:34:51.300
The red detective who called herself
Humanity's Strongest Consultant...

00:34:51.300 --> 00:34:58.840
Solving the case within an inch of its life only after everything
had been resolved and there was no point in doing so.

00:34:58.840 --> 00:35:00.840
And then vanishing into the sunset.

00:35:02.620 --> 00:35:06.640
Like the woman whose real name no one would ever know.

00:35:07.480 --> 00:35:10.420
She...was clearly a genius.

00:35:13.180 --> 00:35:13.880
And...

00:35:15.180 --> 00:35:19.080
And...like Kunagisa Tomo.

00:35:22.560 --> 00:35:24.440
None of it mattered to me.

00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.520
The world went as it would.

00:35:28.020 --> 00:35:32.520
And if it didn't, then it didn't matter to me.

00:35:32.780 --> 00:35:36.120
And if it didn't matter to me then I wasn't interested.

00:35:37.040 --> 00:35:40.860
I had never once wanted to become anything.

00:35:41.420 --> 00:35:43.820
I'd never wanted to accomplish anything.

00:35:44.620 --> 00:35:47.040
I'd wondered if that was a problem...

00:35:47.040 --> 00:35:50.580
But even that question failed to matter to me.

00:35:56.700 --> 00:35:58.280
Some part of me was frozen over.

00:36:00.100 --> 00:36:01.940
No, that wasn't it.

00:36:03.580 --> 00:36:06.080
Some part of me was dried out.

00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:09.220
Apathetic, disinterested.

00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:14.980
Kunagisa Tomo was...my source of moisture.

00:36:18.300 --> 00:36:19.500
Moisture?

00:36:21.560 --> 00:36:23.540
Was that how it worked for you, Shinya?

00:36:24.120 --> 00:36:29.060
The way Sakaki Shinya followed her like a shadow.

00:36:30.400 --> 00:36:36.360
If so, we were much, much too alike.

00:36:39.140 --> 00:36:42.760
I don't know who the world revolves around...

00:36:43.280 --> 00:36:46.140
But the earth revolves around the sun.

00:36:46.680 --> 00:36:49.100
Things were as they were...

00:36:49.740 --> 00:36:51.540
...and would not be otherwise.

00:36:52.340 --> 00:36:54.320
Same went for everyone.

00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:58.500
The truth was always out of reach.

00:36:59.220 --> 00:37:01.660
But I didn't want it, anyway.

00:37:02.780 --> 00:37:05.240
Perhaps that was the problem.

00:37:05.820 --> 00:37:09.940
The laziness Aikawa had accused me of.

00:37:12.140 --> 00:37:14.700
Like I care.

00:37:15.800 --> 00:37:18.580
I don't think about stuff like that all that often...

00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:22.260
I don't care if the world goes the way I want it...

00:37:22.820 --> 00:37:25.520
I don't care to solve the mysteries in it.

00:37:26.440 --> 00:37:29.220
If I see a puzzle in front of me I just get annoyed.

00:37:35.860 --> 00:37:39.000
If I'm still alive tomorrow, that's enough.

00:37:41.140 --> 00:37:47.260
Sorry, Aikawa. But I'm not alive to give the world value.

00:37:48.620 --> 00:37:53.840
If someone asked me why I was alive, I'd say, 'Just in case.'

00:37:54.920 --> 00:37:57.600
That was reason enough to live.

00:37:58.140 --> 00:38:00.540
And that was reason enough for me to live.

00:38:01.160 --> 00:38:03.260
It was reason enough for most of us.

00:38:05.740 --> 00:38:09.540
But. But Kunagisa was different.

00:38:10.520 --> 00:38:12.600
That's all I wanted to say.

00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:19.360
Not that it matters.

00:38:37.520 --> 00:38:40.120
If I didn't see her today, I could see her tomorrow.

00:38:40.720 --> 00:38:42.940
I could see her any time I wanted.

00:38:45.440 --> 00:38:48.300
Five years ago. Before I met Kunagisa Tomo.

00:38:48.820 --> 00:38:50.840
I feel like I had nothing.

00:38:51.840 --> 00:38:59.000
But reunited with her, spending time with her...I still have nothing.

00:39:00.360 --> 00:39:01.200
I'm still empty.

00:39:02.600 --> 00:39:06.000
Like I was trapped in a routine.

00:39:06.680 --> 00:39:08.160
Going through the motions.

00:39:08.560 --> 00:39:09.640
Just living.

00:39:13.460 --> 00:39:14.820
Damn it.

00:39:17.680 --> 00:39:19.700
Okay, okay, I'm going.

00:39:21.820 --> 00:39:22.740
Thus.

00:39:24.220 --> 00:39:27.440
This vague, arbitrary, mechanically indefinite story...

00:39:27.440 --> 00:39:29.160
An average tale of nothing at all...

00:39:29.780 --> 00:39:32.740
With an unnaturally empty certainty at the heart of it...

00:39:32.980 --> 00:39:37.060
...ended anticlimatically like a red red fantasia.

00:39:48.280 --> 00:39:51.420
And I went to Kunagisa's side.

00:39:58.750 --> 00:40:04.290
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:40:04.290 --> 00:40:07.710
Spun around when near you

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:11.050
Leaning towards your right

00:40:11.050 --> 00:40:13.550
What I've got in my hands

00:40:13.550 --> 00:40:16.390
Is not a dream or nothing

00:40:16.390 --> 00:40:20.060
But there's something somewhere

00:40:20.060 --> 00:40:23.100
Throbbing in my heart

00:40:23.100 --> 00:40:26.020
If the one that you do love

00:40:26.020 --> 00:40:30.400
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:40:30.400 --> 00:40:33.110
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:40:33.110 --> 00:40:37.330
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:40:37.330 --> 00:40:39.950
We'd once been so hollow

00:40:39.950 --> 00:40:42.790
Trapped inside that little box

00:40:42.790 --> 00:40:46.290
But now we've seen outside that box

00:40:46.290 --> 00:40:49.510
And have no idea where we are.

00:40:49.960 --> 00:40:51.420
That's all.

00:41:05.310 --> 00:41:07.770
Afterimages of our bliss

00:41:07.770 --> 00:41:10.610
Glimpses of the future

00:41:10.610 --> 00:41:14.150
A glance at something fragile

00:41:14.150 --> 00:41:19.030
Those times that we can still laugh together

00:41:23.900 --> 00:41:31.070
What I lack is everything you have

00:41:31.280 --> 00:41:38.200
What I want to be is everything you want

00:41:38.620 --> 00:41:41.790
The moment we first met

00:41:42.290 --> 00:41:45.290
I'm sure I already knew

00:41:45.290 --> 00:41:49.670
Even before it began

00:41:49.670 --> 00:41:53.380
Behind my words

00:41:53.380 --> 00:41:56.430
I'm always hiding

00:41:56.430 --> 00:42:01.640
Keeping my feelings buried deep

00:42:01.640 --> 00:42:15.570
Now, the world that keeps us trapped sure changes before you know it

00:42:16.450 --> 00:42:24.790
I mean my heart's already dyed a single color,
in my mind the answer's already been chosen

00:42:24.790 --> 00:42:31.210
Is it fate? I don't know, but I'll reach out my hand

00:42:31.210 --> 00:42:34.970
I bet we don't need words at all

00:42:34.970 --> 00:42:38.810
Your melody and my rhythm

00:42:38.810 --> 00:42:43.390
Clamp up our feelings and spin out our fingers

00:42:43.390 --> 00:42:46.770
I'll always be right here

00:42:47.120 --> 00:42:53.050
<i>The Beheading Cycle</i>

00:42:47.120 --> 00:42:53.050
<i>The Blue Savant and
the Master of Nonsense</i>

00:42:47.190 --> 00:42:50.650
Right by your side
